      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "JUNDAH (4) brings the most appealing profile, having placed on debut after being held up before winning by two lengths at Pakenham Synthetic as favourite. She's trialled well enough leading in and has plenty of upside to measure up to these. MISS COTOLETTA (3) is the proven race mare of the main hopes, beaten a neck first-up at Mornington after travelling well and fighting on. She'll take beating again. INVINCIBLE LOVER (5) has been around the mark all campaign and her 1000m record is hard to fault, while first-time blinkers give her a good chance of turning the tables on MISS COTOLETTA who finished narrowly ahead last start. EGERTON (2) is going okay and off a let up since her last run at Cranbourne when finishing fourth. She'll be running on. THE BIRTHDAY PARTY (6) is coming off a smart win in BM56 company and can run well again.",
